{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop. Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, mei.chen@brightline.example, not VIP). Reports she may have left her work laptop in an Uber last night and does not remember whether it was locked. Assigned device: BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15, 512 GB, 75 GB free). Device status: online=true, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:30 UTC (about 9:30 PM Chicago on Oct 10, which is around the time of the ride). No warnings. Sign-in logs (14 days): all successful, normal Chicago locations and hours, last sign-in Oct 9 via VPN, no failed passwords, no MFA denials. Nothing unusual found. Account: active, not blocked, VPN enabled, password last set 2026-09-11. Mailbox 99.4% full (50.9 of 51.2 GB). Actions: requested block_sign_in for user 9 (pending technician approval). Needed from Tier 2: remotely lock or wipe BL-LT-0109 as soon as possible, since it is online and checking in and lock status is unknown. Confirm what data may be on it (local files, cached mail, saved sessions). Then plan a password reset once the user is verified. Police report is not indicated unless the device is confirmed stolen. Reply to the user must not claim anything is done.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation for any lost device. P1. Tier 2 needs to remotely lock or wipe BL-LT-0109, which is online and possibly unlocked."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for reporting this, Mei. I've escalated your lost laptop to our Tier 2 team so they can work on remotely locking or wiping it. I've also requested a block on your work sign-in and VPN access to stop anyone from using a saved session. That block still needs a technician to approve it, so it isn't in effect yet. Please don't try to recover the laptop yourself. If you are able to, check with the rideshare company's lost-and-found, and reply with where and when you think you left it. Tier 2 may contact you to confirm a few details.",
  "internal_note": "P1 lost laptop, KB-021. User: Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, not VIP, active, VPN enabled). Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15): online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:30 UTC (about 9:30 PM Chicago Oct 10, near the ride time), no warnings. Sign-in logs for 14 days show only normal Chicago activity, no failed logins or MFA denials, last sign-in Oct 9. Lock status unknown. Queued block_sign_in (approval_id 1, pending technician approval, not yet run). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) to remotely lock or wipe BL-LT-0109 quickly, since it is online and checking in. Tier 2 should also confirm data exposure. Password reset to be planned after user verification. Mailbox is 99.4% full, which is unrelated but noted.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
